ing) with the worker and its sleep child in the service cgroup.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-6553b93889124e2b\",\"cmd-73b62499dd7f4fb2\",\"cmd-db152d1ff018410b\"]},{\"id\":\"write-confinement\",\"requirement\":\"Service is confined so it writes only inside /var/lib/inventory\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"Directory /var/lib/inventory created and owned by the service's dedicated user; unit uses ProtectSystem=strict with ReadWritePaths=/var/lib/inventory (confirmed via systemctl show on the live unit). Only expected files (count, inventory.log) exist there, owned by inventory-worker. A falsification test using a transient unit with identical sandbox directives showed a write to /etc failing (read-only filesystem) while a write to /var/lib/inventory succeeded, corroborating the confinement is actually enforced rather than merely declared. The falsification ran as a separate transient unit rather than the inventory-worker unit itself, which is a minor indirection but uses matching directives.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-14d2d367a8324c52\",\"cmd-e876848b05b4494c\",\"cmd-a9f51374a0fb4d82\"]},{\"id\":\"no-new-privileges\",\"requirement\":\"Service gains no new privileges\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"Unit defines NoNewPrivileges=yes and an empty CapabilityBoundingSet=; systemctl show on the running unit confirms NoNewPrivileges=yes is actually applied.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-73b62499dd7f4fb2\",\"cmd-e876848b05b4494c\"]}],\"confidence\":0.92,\"operational_hygiene\":{\"score\":0.95,\"summary\":\"Command trace shows a clean, purposeful sequence: user/group creation, data dir, script, unit file, enable/start, and read-only verification, all directly tied to the task. One systemd-run falsification attempt (cmd-84ef636ce88340b6) failed to start (connection reset) and produced no state change. The successful falsification run (cmd-a9f51374a0fb4d82) left a test artifact (/var/lib/inventory/should-succeed) and a transient unit, both of which were explicitly cleaned up immediately afterward (cmd-0ea1e65b024044f8: rm -f should-succeed; systemctl reset-failed inv-test), leaving no residue. The restart protocol used a backgrounded reboot command (cmd-4695f0b789fc4753), a necessary bounded mutation for the independently required node-restart evidence, and left only an expected /tmp/reboot.log artifact. No abandoned files, conflicting services, unsafe exposure, or weakened security controls were observed; after-executor failed-services and package-health checks are clean.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-84ef636ce88340b6\",\"cmd-a9f51374a0fb4d82\",\"cmd-0ea1e65b024044f8\",\"cmd-4695f0b789fc4753\",\"global:after_executor:node1:failed-services\",\"global:after_executor:node1:package-health\"]},\"overall_summary\":\"The executor deployed inventory-worker as a properly confined, enabled, and running systemd service on node1, with directly observed evidence that NoNewPrivileges is applied and that writes are actually restricted to /var/lib/inventory via a falsification test. The independently required node-restart evidence protocol was also completed with a full pre-restart baseline, an acknowledged reboot, a directly observed change in boot identity (636556ce... -> c8000397...), and post-restart confirmation that the service is enabled/active and that its persisted counter/log data survived and continued incrementing. Operational hygiene is high: a failed transient-unit attempt caused no mutation, and the one test artifact created during falsification was promptly cleaned up.\",\"limitations\":[\"The confinement falsification test ran against a separate transient systemd-run unit configured with matching sandbox directives rather than against the actual inventory-worker.service unit, so it is strong corroborating evidence rather than a direct test of the deployed service instance.\",\"Restart evidence relies on connectivity gaps (timeouts/connection reset) as an implicit signal the node was down, rather than a direct 'node unreachable' state capture, though the subsequent boot_id change and service recovery are directly observed.\"]}","structured_output":{"requirements":[{"id":"managed-service","requirement":"Run a long-running background worker as a managed systemd service named inventory-worker on node1","status":"satisfied","summary":"Unit file /etc/systemd/system/inventory-worker.service created with an infinite tick-loop ExecStart, verified clean by systemd-analyze verify, enabled and started; systemctl status shows Active: active (running) with the worker and its sleep child in the service cgroup.","evidence_ids":["cmd-6553b93889124e2b","cmd-73b62499dd7f4fb2","cmd-db152d1ff018410b"]},{"id":"write-confinement","requirement":"Service is confined so it writes only inside /var/lib/inventory","status":"satisfied","summary":"Directory /var/lib/inventory created and owned by the service's dedicated user; unit uses ProtectSystem=strict with ReadWritePaths=/var/lib/inventory (confirmed via systemctl show on the live unit). Only expected files (count, inventory.log) exist there, owned by inventory-worker. A falsification test using a transient unit with identical sandbox directives showed a write to /etc failing (read-only filesystem) while a write to /var/lib/inventory succeeded, corroborating the confinement is actually enforced rather than merely declared. The falsification ran as a separate transient unit rather than the inventory-worker unit itself, which is a minor indirection but uses matching directives.","evidence_ids":["cmd-14d2d367a8324c52","cmd-e876848b05b4494c","cmd-a9f51374a0fb4d82"]},{"id":"no-new-privileges","requirement":"Service gains no new privileges","status":"satisfied","summary":"Unit defines NoNewPrivileges=yes and an empty CapabilityBoundingSet=; systemctl show on the running unit confirms NoNewPrivileges=yes is actually applied.","evidence_ids":["cmd-73b62499dd7f4fb2","cmd-e876848b05b4494c"]}],"confidence":0.92,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.95,"summary":"Command trace shows a clean, purposeful sequence: user/group creation, data dir, script, unit file, enable/start, and read-only verification, all directly tied to the task. One systemd-run falsification attempt (cmd-84ef636ce88340b6) failed to start (connection reset) and produced no state change. The successful falsification run (cmd-a9f51374a0fb4d82) left a test artifact (/var/lib/inventory/should-succeed) and a transient unit, both of which were explicitly cleaned up immediately afterward (cmd-0ea1e65b024044f8: rm -f should-succeed; systemctl reset-failed inv-test), leaving no residue. The restart protocol used a backgrounded reboot command (cmd-4695f0b789fc4753), a necessary bounded mutation for the independently required node-restart evidence, and left only an expected /tmp/reboot.log artifact. No abandoned files, conflicting services, unsafe exposure, or weakened security controls were observed; after-executor failed-services and package-health checks are clean.","evidence_ids":["cmd-84ef636ce88340b6","cmd-a9f51374a0fb4d82","cmd-0ea1e65b024044f8","cmd-4695f0b789fc4753","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"The executor deployed inventory-worker as a properly confined, enabled, and running systemd service on node1, with directly observed evidence that NoNewPrivileges is applied and that writes are actually restricted to /var/lib/inventory via a falsification test. The independently required node-restart evidence protocol was also completed with a full pre-restart baseline, an acknowledged reboot, a directly observed change in boot identity (636556ce... -> c8000397...), and post-restart confirmation that the service is enabled/active and that its persisted counter/log data survived and continued incrementing. Operational hygiene is high: a failed transient-unit attempt caused no mutation, and the one test artifact created during falsification was promptly cleaned up.","limitations":["The confinement falsification test ran against a separate transient systemd-run unit configured with matching sandbox directives rather than against the actual inventory-worker.service unit, so it is strong corroborating evidence rather than a direct test of the deployed service instance.","Restart evidence relies on connectivity gaps (timeouts/connection reset) as an implicit signal the node was down, rather than a direct 'node unreachable' state capture, though the subsequent boot_id change and service recovery are directly observed."]},"ttft_ms":14347,"type":"result","duration_ms":43612,"uuid":"92b22219-538e-44c5-b8ff-b73e3568f864","ttft_stream_ms":1244,"time_to_request_ms":257,"first_content_frame_ms":1244,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
